          %h3#relation_with_comonoid Relation with comonoid
          %ol
            %li
              %p The simplex category \Delta, whose objects are {1,2,3..n} and morphisms are nondecreasing functions, is the UNIVERSAL “category equipped with a monoid”.
            %li
              %p Dually, \Delta^op is the UNIVERSAL “category equipped with a comonoid”.
            %li
              %p For a group G, there’s an adjunction between (G-reps) and (Vector Spaces) by the forgetful functor and the free G-rep functor. The composition gives you a COMONAD of (G-rep).
            %li
              %p A comonad is just a categorification of a comonoid. More concretely a comonad is a comonoid in End( (G-rep), (G-rep) ).
            %li
              %p Since \Delta^op is has a universal comonoid, we connect both contexts naturally. No wonder there’s nice cohomology theory for groups!
          %p (ref: Categories-for-the-Working-Mathematician-[Mac-Lane])
          %h3#StructuredCohomology Structured group cohomology (topological groups and Lie groups)
          %p
            If the groups in question are not plain groups (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"}> group object
            s internal to
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
          %p
            In parts of the literature cohomology of structured groups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is defined in direct generalization of the formulas above as homotopy classes of morphisms from the simplicial object
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mi G
                    %mo ×
                    %mi G
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mo ⟶
                      %mo ⟶
                    %mi G
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ⟶
                    %mo *
                    %mo )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\left(
                  \\cdots G \times G\stackrel{\longrightarrow}{\stackrel{\longrightarrow}{\longrightarrow}}G \stackrel{\longrightarrow}{\longrightarrow} *
                  \\right)
          %p
            to a simplicial object
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi n
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N (\mathbf{B}^n A)
          %p
            This is what is described
            %a{:href => "#InLowDegree"} above
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+groups"} discrete groups
            %strong not
            in general give the right answer for structured groups: while the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi W
                    %mo ¯
                  %mi G
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi G
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mo ×
                        %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{W}G = G^{\times^\bullet}
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+object"} cofibrant
            in the relevant model category presenting the ambient
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Disc%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Disc∞Grpd
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a structured group the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial object
            given by the same formula is not in general already cofibrant. It needs to be further resolved, instead.
          %p
            Specifically, for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mi G
                    %mo ×
                    %mi G
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mo ⟶
                      %mo ⟶
                    %mi G
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ⟶
                    %mo *
                    %mo )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\left(
                  \\cdots G \times G\stackrel{\longrightarrow}{\stackrel{\longrightarrow}{\longrightarrow}}G \stackrel{\longrightarrow}{\longrightarrow} *
                  \\right)
          %p
            has to be considered as an
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} Lie ∞-groupoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            such as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
            %strong not
            both cofibrant and fibrant. To that extent plain morphisms out of this object do
            %strong not
            compute the correct
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+hom-space"} derived hom-space
          %p Doing requires more work. This is discussed at
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group+cohomology"} Lie group cohomology
          %p
            See below at
            %em
              %a{:href => "#ReferencesOnStructuredGroupCohomology"} References - For structured groups
            for pointers to the literature.
          %h3#NonabelianGroupCohomology Nonabelian group cohomology
          %p
            If the coefficient group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            is nonabelian, its higher
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^n K
            do not exist. But
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-groupoid"} n-groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            with coefficients in these is called
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+group+cohomology"} nonabelian group cohomology
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schreier+theory"} Schreier theory
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#specific_examples Specific examples
          %h4#simple_examples Simple examples
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/carrying"} carrying
          %h4#cohomology_of_
            Cohomology of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 2
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2\mathbb{Z}
          %p
            For group cohomology of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+of+order+2"} group of order 2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 2
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_2 = \mathbb{Z}/2\mathbb{Z}
            see at
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Groupprops"} Groupprops
            %em
              %a{:href => "http://groupprops.subwiki.org/wiki/Group_cohomology_of_cyclic_group:Z2"} Group cohomology of cyclic group Z2
          %h4#cohomology_of__2
            Cohomology of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mn 2
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_2^n
          %p
            The cohomology of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mn 2
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_2^n
            with coefficients in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_2
            admits a very simple description (see (
            %a{:href => "#AM04finite"}> p.66 of Adem &amp; Milgram (2004)
            )). There exists a ring isomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mn 2
                    %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H^{\bullet} (\mathbb{Z}_2^n ,\mathbb{Z}_2 ) \cong \mathbb{Z}_2 [e_1 ,\cdots,e_n ]
          %p
            of the cohomology ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mn 2
                    %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^n (\mathbb{Z}_2^n,\mathbb{Z}_2 )
            to the polynomial ring of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            commuting variables with coefficients in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mn 2
                    %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^q (\mathbb{Z}_2^n,\mathbb{Z}_2 )
            is generated by the classes of the functions:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %msubsup
                    %mi x
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi ⋯
                  %msubsup
                    %mi x
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mi q
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (x^{(1)},\cdots, x^{(q)} )\mapsto x^{(1)}_{i_1}\cdots x^{(q)}_{i_q}
          %p
            with
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ≤
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_1 \leq \cdots \leq i_q
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mn 2
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^{(j)}\in \mathbb{Z}_2^n
            is an
            = succeed "-tuple" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msubsup
                      %mi x
                      %mi n
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x^{(j)}_1 ,\cdots, x^{(j)}_n )
          %h4#cohomology_of___etc
            Cohomology of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(n)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(n)
          %p
            We consider for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
            such as
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+group"} unitary group
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(n)
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+unitary+group"} special unitary group
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi SU
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(n)
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+group"} symplectic group
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp(n)
          %p
            the corresponding group cohomology in terms of the cohomology of the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B G
          %p
            For all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            we have
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi H
                            %mo •
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi BU
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ;
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msub
                            %mi c
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi c
                            %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi H
                            %mo •
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi BSU
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ;
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msub
                            %mi c
                            %mn 2
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi c
                            %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi H
                            %mo •
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi BSp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ;
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msub
                            %mi p
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi p
                            %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  H^\bullet(BU(n);\mathbb{Z}) &amp;= \mathbb{Z}[c_1,\cdots,c_n]
                  \\\
                  H^\bullet(BSU(n);\mathbb{Z}) &amp;= \mathbb{Z}[c_2,\cdots,c_n]
                  \\\
                  H^\bullet(BSp(n);\mathbb{Z}) &amp;= \mathbb{Z}[p_1,\cdots,p_n]
                  \\end{aligned}
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mi i
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_i\in H^{2i}
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mn 4
                        %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_i\in H^{4i}
          %h4#heisenberg_cocycle Heisenberg cocycle
          %p
            The additive group on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^2
            with group operation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo +
                  %mi a
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo +
                  %mi b
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (a,b) + (a',b') = (a + a' , b + b')
          %p
            carries a degree-2 group cocycle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            with values in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\omega : ((a_1,b_1), (a_2,b_2)) \mapsto a_1 \cdot b_2
                  \\,.
          %p The cocycle condition for this is the identity
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 3
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  a_1 \cdot (b_2 + b_3) + a_2 \cdot b_3
                  \=
                  a_1 \cdot b_2 + (a_1 + a_2) \cdot b_3
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+extension"} group extension
            classified by this cocycle is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heisenberg+group"} Heisenberg group
          %h4#galileo_2cocycle Galileo 2-cocycle
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galileo+2-cocycle"} Galileo 2-cocycle
          %h3#classes_of_examples Classes of examples
          %h4#galois_cohomology Galois cohomology
          %p
            The group cohomology of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+groups"} Galois groups
            is called
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+cohomology"} Galois cohomology
          %h4#lie_algebra_cohomology Lie algebra cohomology
          %p
            We may regard a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+object"} infinitesimal
            group. Under this perspective
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cohomology"} Lie algebra cohomology
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-Lie+algebra+cohomology"} infinity-Lie algebra cohomology
            is a special case of (higher) group cohomology. See there for details.
