          %ul
            %li#Milne17
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Milne"}> James Milne
              , Section 15 (16 in the pdf) of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Algebraic Groups
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/9781316711736"} doi:10.1017/9781316711736
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.jmilne.org/math/Books/iag.html"} webpage
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.jmilne.org/math/CourseNotes/iAG200.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            On
            = succeed "-methods:" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+G.+Dwyer"}> William G. Dwyer
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hans-Werner+Henn"} Hans-Werner Henn
              = succeed "," do
                %em Homotopy Theoretic Methods in Group Cohomology
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-0348-8356-6"} doi:10.1007/978-3-0348-8356-6
          %p Further exposition:
          %ul
            %li#Conrad
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brian+Conrad"}> Brian Conrad
                \:
                %em Group cohomology and group extensions
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://math.stanford.edu/~conrad/210BPage/handouts/gpext.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Conrad-GroupCohomologyExtensions.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alejandro+Adem"}> Alejandro Adem
                ,
                %em Lectures on the cohomology of finite groups
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uic.edu/~bshipley/ConMcohomology1.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#Epa10
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Narthana+Epa"}> Narthana Epa
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Platonic 2-groups
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.ms.unimelb.edu.au/documents/thesis/Epa-Platonic2-Groups.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            An introduction to group cohomology of a group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            as the cohomology of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B G
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Joshua Roberts,
                %em Group cohomology: a classifying space perspective
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.piedmont.edu/math/jroberts/notes/qualifyingtalk.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %em Advanced course on classifying spaces and cohomology of groups
                (
                %a{:href => "www-irma.u-strasbg.fr/~henn/notes.ps"}> ps
                )
          %p
            Discussion of the cohomology of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+groups"} discrete groups
            with abelian coefficients in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+modules"} crossed modules
            instead of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
            (an intermediate step in the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
          %ul
            %li
              R. Brown, P. Higgins, R. Sivera,
              %em Nonabelian algebraic topology
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.bangor.ac.uk/%7Emas010/pdffiles/rbrsbookb-e040609.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.bangor.ac.uk/~mas010/nonab-a-t.html"} web
          %p
            Cohomology of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+groups"} simplicial groups
            is discussed for instance in
          %ul
            %li
              Sebastian Thomas,
              %em On the second cohomology group of a simplicial group
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.rwth-aachen.de/~Sebastian.Thomas/publications/Thomas_On_the_second_cohomology_group_of_a_simplicial_group.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            Much of what is called “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"}> nonabelian cohomology
            ” in the existing literature concerns the case of nonabelian group cohomology with coefficients in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+2-group"} automorphism 2-group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi AUT
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AUT(H)
            of some possibly nonabelian group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
          %p
            This is the topic of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schreier+theory"} Schreier theory
          %p A random example for this use of terminology would be
          %ul
            %li
              Roggenkamp, Scott,
              %em Automorphisms and nonabelian cohomology
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.virginia.edu/~lls2l/automorphisms_and_nonabelian.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p For a conceptual discussion of nonabelian group cohomology see
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"} Mike Shulman
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lectures+on+n-Categories+and+Cohomology"} Lectures on n-Categories and Cohomology
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0608420"}> arXiv
              )
          %p
            Group cocycles classify
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+extensions"} group extensions
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-group"} 2-group
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-groups"} infinity-groups
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+complexes"} crossed complexes
            %em strict
            = succeed "-groups," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Johannes+Huebschmann"}> Johannes Huebschmann
              ,
              %em
                Crossed
                = succeed "-fold" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              (
              %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/BF02566688"}> web
              )
          %h3#ReferencesOnStructuredGroupCohomology On structured group cohomology
          %p In
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"}> Jim Stasheff
              ,
              %em Continuous cohomology of groups and classifying spaces
              Bull. Amer. Math. Soc. Volume 84, Number 4 (1978), 513-530 (
              %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/DPubS?service=UI&version=1.0&verb=Display&handle=euclid.bams/1183540920"}> web
              )
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            \-cocycles on a topological group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            with values in a topological abelian group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            are considered as continuous maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi G
                    %mrow
                      %mo ×
                      %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G^{\times n}\to A
            (p. 3 ).
          %p
            A definition in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} Ext-functors
            and comparison with the naive definition is in
          %ul
            %li
              David Wigner,
              %em Algebraic cohomology of topological groups
              Transactions of the American Mathematical Society, volume 178 (1973)(
              %a{:href => "http://egg.epfl.ch/~nmonod/bonn/Wigner_1973.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p A classical reference that considers the cohomology of Lie groups as topological spaces is
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Armand+Borel"}> Armand Borel
              ,
              %em Homology and cohomology of compact connected Lie groups
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC1063923/pdf/pnas01596-0040.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p A corrected definition of topological group cohomology has been given by Segal
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"}> Graeme Segal
                ,
                %em Cohomology of topological groups
                In Symposia Mathematica, Vol. IV (INDAM, Rome, 1968/69), pages 377{387. Academic Press, London, (1970).
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"}> Graeme Segal
                ,
                %em A classifying space of a topological group in the sense of Gel’fand-Fuks. Funkcional. Anal. i Prilozen.,
              %p 9(2):48{50, (1975).
          %p
            For
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reductive+algebraic+groups"} reductive algebraic groups
          %ul
            %li#HKLV98
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H%C3%A9l%C3%A8ne+Esnault"}> Hélène Esnault
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bruno+Kahn"} Bruno Kahn
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marc+Levine"} Marc Levine
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eckart+Viehweg"} Eckart Viehweg
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Arason invariant and mod 2 algebraic cycles
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://www.uni-due.de/~bm0032/publ/Arason.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/journals/jams/1998-11-01/S0894-0347-98-00248-3/"} publisher page
          %h3#OnTopologicalGroups On various topological groups
          %p
            Some references pertaining to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            of the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B G
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+class"}> characteristic class
            es).
          %h4#compact_lie_groups Compact Lie groups
          %p
            Cohomology of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B G
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
            underlying a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
          %ul#MilnorStasheff
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Milnor"}> John Milnor
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} Jim Stasheff
              %em Characteristic Classes
              , Princeton University Press and University of Tokyo Press, Princeton, New Jersey, (1974).
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Mark Feshbach,
                %em Some General Theorems on the Cohomology of Classifying Spaces of Compact Lie Groups
                Transactions of the American Mathematical Society Vol. 264, No. 1 (Mar., 1981), pp. 49-58 (
                %a{:href => "http://www.jstor.org/stable/1998409"}> JSTOR
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Donald+Yau"}> Donald Yau
                ,
                %em Cohomology of unitary and symplectic groups
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.mathnet.ru/links/c8897bc54ec0a1a49d03ca681d53db7b/ljm147.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                D. Benson,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Greenlees"} John Greenlees
                %em Commutative algebra for cohomology rings of classifying spaces of compact Lie groups
                (
                %a{:href => "http://hopf.math.purdue.edu/Benson-Greenlees/Liegroupca.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Friedlander"}> Eric Friedlander
                , Guido Mislin,
                %em Cohomology of classifying spaces of complex Lie groups and related discrete groups
                Commentarii Mathematici Helvetici
              %p Volume 59, Number 1, 347-361,
          %h4#the_unitary_groups_
            The unitary groups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(n)
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+group"} unitary group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+cohomology"} integral cohomology
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B U(n)
            consists of the
            = succeed "es," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+class"} Chern class
          %h4#the_special_orthogonal_groups__
            The (special) orthogonal groups
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(n)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(n)
          %p
            The cohomology of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BO%28n%29"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B O(n)
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+group"}> orthogonal group
            ) and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BSO%28n%29"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mi S
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B S O(n)
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+orthogonal+group"}> special orthogonal group
            ) with coefficients in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_2
            is discussed in (
            %a{:href => "#MilnorStasheff"}> MilnorStasheff, 1974
            ).
          %p
            The cohomology of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BO%28n%29"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B O(n)
            with coefficients in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_{2 m}
            was found in
          %ul
            %li
              Emery Thomas ,
              %em
                On the cohomology of the real Grassman complexes and the characteristic classes of the
                = succeed "-plane" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              , Trans. Amer. Math. Soc. 96 (1960), 67–89.
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-structure" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                E. Brown (Jr.),
                %em
                  The cohomology of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                        %mi SO
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B SO(n)
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                        %mi O
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B O(n)
                  with integer coefficients
                Proc. AMS Soc. 85 (1982)
            %li
              %p
                Mark Feshbach,
                %em
                  The integral cohomology rings of the classifying spaces of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi O
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(n)
                  and
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi SO
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(n)
          %p
            For
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} local coefficients
            see
          %ul
            %li#Cadek99
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+%C4%8Cadek"}> Martin Čadek
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    The cohomology of
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi B
                          %mi O
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B O(n)
                    with twisted integer coefficients
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.kjm/1250517912"} Euclid
            %li
              %p
                Richard Lastovecki,
                %em
                  Cohomology of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                        %mi O
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ×
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ×
                        %mi B
                        %mi O
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mi m
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B O(n_1) \times \cdots \times B O(n_m)
                  with local integer coefficients
                Comment.Math.Univ.Carolin. 46,1 (2005)21–32 (
                %a{:href => "http://www.emis.de/journals/CMUC/pdf/cmuc0501/lastovec.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %h4#for_spingroup_stringgroup_ For spin-group, string-group, …
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead+tower"} Whitehead tower
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+group"} orthogonal group
            starts out with
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fivebrane+group"} fivebrane group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo →
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+group"} string group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo →
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+group"} spin group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo →
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+orthogonal+group"} special orthogonal group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo →
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+group"} orthogonal group
          %p
            Group cohomology of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+group"} spin group
            (cohomology of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mi Spin
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B Spin
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Emery Thomas,
                %em On the cohomology groups of the classifying space for the stable spinor group
                , Bol. Soc. Mex. (1962), 57 - 69
            %li
              %p
                Masana Harada, Akira Kono,
                %em
                  Cohomology mod 2 of the classifying space of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Spin
                          %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin^c(n)
                Publications of the Research Institute for Mathematical Sciences archive Volume 22 Issue 3, Sept. (1986) (
                %a{:href => "http://dl.acm.org/citation.cfm?id=23393"}> web
                )
          %p
            Group cohomology of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+group"} string group
            (cohomology of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mi String
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B String
          %ul
            %li
              %em On the integral cohomology of the seven-connective cover of B O
              Bull. Austral. Math. Soc. Vol 38 (1988) (
              %a{:href => "http://journals.cambridge.org/download.php?file=%2FBAZ%2FBAZ38_01%2FS0004972700027179a.pdf&code=8374f17b7aa6ffb83f42f347c677729f"}> pdf
              )
          %h4#the_exceptional_lie_groups The exceptional Lie groups
          %p
            Cohomology of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exceptional+Lie+group"} exceptional Lie group
          %ul
            %li
              Akira Kono, Mamoru Mimura,
              %em
                Cohomology mod 3 of the classifying space of the Lie group
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mn 6
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_6
              , Math. Scand. 46 (1980) (
              %a{:href => "http://www.mscand.dk/article.php?id=2533"}> pdf
              )
          %h4#loop_groups_of_compact_lie_groups Loop groups of compact Lie groups
          %ul
            %li
              Daisuke Kishimoto, Akira Kono,
              %em Cohomology of the classifying spaces of loop groups
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.kyoto-u.ac.jp/preprint/2004/13kishimoto.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %h3#online_references Online references
          %p Some of the above materiel is taken from discussion at
          %ul
            %li
              MO,
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/questions/75389/group-cohomology-of-compact-lie-group-with-integer-coeffient"} Group cohomology of compact Lie group with integer coeffient
        .revisedby
